TY  - JOUR
TI  - Rapid End-to-End Test Generation and Hallucination Mitigation Using Generative Artificial Intelligence
AU  - C. Barathidass
AU  - K. Namburu
T2  - IEEE Access
AB  - End-to-end testing of distributed systems remains constrained by rapidly evolving architectures and maintenance requirements. Previous template-based solutions required months of engineering effort and lacked scalability owing to Document Object Model (DOM) selector fragility. This study proposes a novel single-shot testing methodology using abstract-class-based DOM referencing combined with operation-specific prompt templates for Create, Read, Update, and Delete workflows. In contrast to conventional chain-of-thought prompting, which requires multiple iterations, our approach eliminates complex reasoning chains while standardizing large language model outputs through structured abstraction layers. Empirical validation across 15 services generated over 900 test cases, reducing the manual effort from weeks to approximately 4 h per service while achieving 80%–90% accuracy. In addition, error analysis revealed typical distributions, with the most frequent failures being the selector mismatches and the absent assertions. The framework was implemented by a single engineer in one week, compared to the months required for template-based systems. This methodology advances automated quality assurance and test case generation by balancing abstraction and specificity for rapid baseline coverage in cloud-native environments. This verification shows the scalability of the methodology and the versatility of the approach in many enterprise situations, including the foundation of future benchmarking as well as adaptive abstraction methodologies.
