AU  - K. Mitsuhashi
AU  - I. Sekita
AU  - H. Takeshita
T2  - 2026 IEEE 2nd International Conference on Consumer Technology (ICCT-Pacific)
AB  - The widespread use of smartphones and generative AI has led to a shortage of personnel capable of performing advanced PC operations, such as specialized diagramming, required in a DX (Digital Transformation) society. Despite this, there is a strong demand for creating business diagrams, such as organizational charts. This research proposes and develops a business diagramming tool utilizing Augmented Reality (AR) technology and physical blocks and investigates its effectiveness in terms of creation time and user experience. The tool's operation is designed to be more intuitive and easier than conventional PC-based methods. By arranging these physical blocks within the camera's view, users can create SWOT analysis diagrams (four-quadrant diagrams), organizational charts, and Gantt charts. The tool's effectiveness is subsequently validated through sample creation tasks while referencing existing diagrams. In this result, AR-based operation enables faster diagram creation compared to PC-based methods, and the tool is more intuitive and easier to understand.
