AU  - R. Bie
AU  - W. Wei
AU  - Y. Li
T2  - 2025 5th International Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Robotics, and Communication (ICAIRC)
AB  - To enhance the intelligent processing capability of knowledge in the wind power domain, this paper proposes a framework for constructing and applying a wind power knowledge graph based on a Multimodal Large Language Model (MLLM). This framework integrates multimodal data such as text and images, utilizes the MLLM to simultaneously extract image content and structural information, and introduces a Chain-of-Thought guided reasoning mechanism. Through mod-ules including sliding window overlapping chunking, multi-step question generation, and step recognition with quality verification, a high-quality wind power knowledge graph is constructed. Furthermore, the graph is applied to query decomposition and agent planning, extending its applications to scenarios such as fault diagnosis and intelligent maintenance. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed framework significantly outper-forms both pure Retrieval-Augmented Generation and pure knowledge graph methods in terms of the comprehensiveness, diversity, and empowerment of knowledge processing.
