AB  - We present a knowledge-driven framework that enhances large language models (LLMs) through dynamic integration of knowledge graph (KG) structures. Our approach addresses the challenge of balancing domain-specific knowledge with linguistic flexibility by injecting KG-derived augmentation structures into LLM prompts. The framework features a multi-dimensional evaluation system assessing both direct aspects and indirect utility of generated texts. Evaluations using the Unified Medical Language System (UMLS) demonstrate our method's effectiveness in producing human-like, factually accurate content while significantly expanding knowledge coverage and enhancing specialist capabilities without degrading general performance. This work provides a scalable solution for reliable synthetic data generation in specialized domains.
