TY  - CONF
TI  - A Multi-Scale Adaptive Retrieval-Augmented Generation Framework with Semantic and Structural Knowledge Graphs
AU  - F. Ning
AU  - Y. Bai
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Communication Networks and Machine Learning (CNML)
AB  - The combination of large language models and retrieval augmented generation (RAG) demonstrates great potential in complex multi-hop reasoning and long document question answering tasks. However, the existing RAG methods still face two key challenges: Firstly, there is the issue of determining the appropriate context range in the retrieval stage. An overly long context may introduce redundant information and interfere with the modeling of key information, while an overly short context may miss important facts and affect the accuracy of the generated results. Secondly, the existing methods perform well in single-fact question answering tasks, but their performance is still limited in complex scenarios such as multi-hop reasoning and cross-paragraph evidence integration.This paper proposes a multi-scale adaptive retrieval-enhanced generation framework based on both semantic and structural knowledge graphs. In this framework, the structural knowledge graph is centered around different granularity levels such as chapters, paragraphs, and sentences, to support flexible and adjustable context slicing. The semantic knowledge graph models entities and their relationships in the form of triples, and uses entity cross-connections to achieve semantic associations across paragraphs, effectively enhancing the completeness of evidence retrieval. The experimental results on the HotpotQA dataset show that, compared with the existing mainstream RAG methods, our method has achieved stable improvements in both retrieval quality and answer generation quality, verifying the effectiveness of the proposed method in complex multi-hop question answering tasks.
