AB  - Software development cycles frequently suffer from bottlenecks in requirements engineering, design consistency, and security auditing. This paper explores the integration of Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) across the Agile Scrum methodology to automate these traditionally labor-intensive phases. It proposes a structured framework that evolved from a basic messaging prototype into a comprehensive web application, utilizing multi-agent collaborative systems like MetaGPT. By synchronizing the transition from high-level user stories to production-ready code, the proposed framework demonstrates that AI-assisted workflows can significantly reduce development time. Comparative benchmarking of state-of-the-art Large Language Models (LLMs)—ranging from paid tiers like GPT-4 to local open-source models via Ollama—reveals a clear trade-off between architectural accuracy and operational cost. Findings indicate a 55.8% increase in coding speed and the ability to detect up to 75% of common defects, underscoring the potential of GenAI while emphasizing the continued need for human oversight in security contexts.
