AB  - This study proposes a method to assist the specification of requirements for generating state transition diagrams indispensable for reinforcement learning. It provides templates and precautions to assist inexperienced engineers in refining their requirements so that the requirements can be semi-automatically converted into state transition diagrams. The effectiveness of various assistive elements is evaluated by comparing edit distances pre- and post-modification. The method also applies the same assistance to LLMs to analyze differences in human performance. Experiments on specifying the card game “Old Maid” confirm the effectiveness of model requirements and precautions. The results reveal the effectiveness of model documents and precautions, but no significant effect with the precaution position. They also show the superiority of LLM for the target problem fully explained on the Internet.
