AU  - A. B. V
AU  - R. Kumar.J.S.
AU  - N. V. Babu
T2  - 2025 9th International Conference on Electronics, Communication and Aerospace Technology (ICECA)
AB  - Software engineering automation remains constrained, with existing AI tools typically focusing on isolated tasks such as code generation, while still relying heavily on human intervention for integration, testing, and deployment. This paper presents a multi-agent system that will autonomously manage the whole software development process-including natural language requirements to deployed systems. The system leverages a Semantic Kernel for dynamic task decomposition and orchestrates specialized, role-specific agents for code generation, testing, debugging, and deployment. A vector-based knowledge retention engine allows for ongoing learning and reuse of solutions across projects. This will ensure high-quality code and consistent architecture. The framework works with professional tools like Docker and GitHub Actions. It supports results that are ready for production. In experimental tests, the end-to-end task success rate reached 65 percent. The average development time dropped to 35 minutes. There was also a decrease in human intervention compared to baseline systems like ChatDev and GPT-4, which relied on manual tools. This work creates a new approach in autonomous software engineering. It uses coordinated multi-agent systems that can handle complex projects with minimal human involvement.
