AU  - J. Benita
AU  - S. P. S.
AU  - H. P. K.
AU  - V. K. S.
AU  - V. V.
T2  - 2026 IEEE International Conference on Emerging Computing and Intelligent Technologies (ICoECIT)
AB  - The integration of large language models (LLMs) into healthcare holds immense promise for clinical support, research, and patient care. However, the critical issue of factual inaccuracies, or "hallucinations," and the high-stakes nature of medical decisions necessitate a new development paradigm focused on trustworthiness. This paper presents a comprehensive blueprint for 'Medi GPT,' a specialized medical LLM. Our approach addresses key architectural limitations and trustworthiness gaps by proposing a novel fine-tuning objective, the Fact-Grounded Distillation Objective (FGDO). The FGDO leverages an external medical knowledge base to directly penalize and correct factual errors during training, providing a robust mechanism for ensuring truthfulness. We detail the methodology for data curation from high-quality public datasets, the development of a custom, domain-specific tokenizer, and the use of the Attention with Linear Biases (ALiBi) technique to efficiently handle long clinical documents. The paper also outlines a comprehensive evaluation strategy that goes beyond standard benchmarks to include adversarial testing and expert-led human review, thereby ensuring the model's clinical robustness and safety. This work represents a crucial step toward building AI systems that are not only powerful but also reliable, transparent, and ethically sound for clinical use.
