TI  - Leveling Up Software Project Management Education: From Manual Mastery to AI Empowerment
AU  - S. K. Tunç
T2  - 2025 10th International Conference on Computer Science and Engineering (UBMK)
AB  - The integration of generative artificial intelligence (AI) tools, particularly large language models, into software engineering education presents both significant opportunities and pedagogical challenges. A central concern lies in achieving an effective balance between leveraging AI-driven efficiencies and maintaining the development of critical thinking and practical skills. This study introduces a two-phase instructional framework. In the initial phase, students undertake core project planning tasks manually to establish foundational competencies. In the subsequent phase, they employ AI tools during a capstone exercise designed to simulate real-world scenarios. The model was implemented within an undergraduate software project management course. Observations from the first phase indicated recurring challenges in visual planning tasks, which informed the selection and application of AI tools in the second phase. Student reflections suggest enhanced proficiency in AI usage and prompt engineering; however, ethical awareness remained limited. The findings underscore the value of a scaffolded pedagogical approach that emphasizes manual mastery prior to AI adoption and provide a replicable framework for cultivating AI literacy aligned with industry expectations in software engineering education.
