TI  - Agentic Symbolic Learning for Deterministic and Granular Clinical Data Normalization
AU  - B. J. de Urries
AU  - D. Gómez Ortiz
AU  - E. Menasalvas
T2  - 2026 IEEE Conference on Artificial Intelligence (CAI)
AB  - Every day hospitals produce a vast amount of Electronic Health Records (EHRs) that contain unstructured clinical data essential for research. Deep learning plays an important role in extracting knowledge from unstructured data. While transformers models, particularly BERT-based architectures, have demonstrated State-of-the-Art (SOTA) performance in Named Entity Recognition (NER), they function primarily as sequence labeler, often failing to produce the granular, standardized structures required for downstream analytics (e.g., decomposing a complex string into its prefix, category, and numeric components). This paper presents a Hybrid Neuro-Symbolic Framework for structuring clinical data.Our approach utilizes a two-stage pipeline: First, a fine-tuned BERT-based model performs the high-recall extraction of medical entities from oncological text, specifically Cancer TNM stages and molecular markers. Second, these raw entity spans are processed by a Self-Correcting Agentic Graph. This graph, orchestrated with Large Language Models (LLMs), validates the extracted data according to clinical guidelines (AJCC) and biomarkers, synthesizes context-aware Regex patterns for granular parsing, and builds a semantic dictionary for value standardization. We demonstrate that this hybrid approach combines the extraction power of transformer-based architectures with the semantic rigor and interpretability of symbolic reasoning.
