AU  - J. P. S. Simão
AU  - L. S. R. Machado
AU  - J. B. Da Silva
AU  - P. A. Behar
T2  - 2025 IEEE Smart World Congress (SWC)
AB  - This paper presents the design and proof-of-concept of a conversational agent integrated into a competence management system to assist students in competence development. The agent leverages Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) to provide tailored feedback and recommend learning strategies based on students’ proficiency levels. The proposed system includes a structured competence management system, a recommendation engine, and an interactive chatbot that engages users in guided learning experiences. The architecture of the system is built using Django, PostgreSQL, and OpenAI’s API, ensuring a scalable and adaptable solution for different learning contexts. The agent is designed to be integrated with Learning Management Systems (LMS) via LTI and employs the xAPI standard to track user interactions. Through a structured interaction model, students receive custom responses that foster self-regulated learning. While the application demonstrates potential for competence development, its effectiveness must be validated through real-user testing. Future research will focus on usability evaluations and refining AI-driven recommendations to enhance educational outcomes.
